    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe startup warmup requests set `temperature` to 0. `SamplingParams` changes this to `top_k=1`, so the batch is `is_all_greedy` and the sampler runs `torch.argmax`. The warmup does not call FlashInfer sampling, so `get_sampling_module()` does not load the FlashInfer `sampling` module.\n\nThe first user request that sets top-k, top-p, or min-p loads the module. If `flashinfer-jit-cache` is not installed (the Docker default is `INSTALL_FLASHINFER_JIT_CACHE=0`), FlashInfer compiles `sampling.cu` with nvcc during that request.\n\nWe observed a 60 s stall on the first request without this change.\n\n## Modifications\n\nThe warmup requests now send `top_k: 2` in place of `temperature: 0`. This applies to the `/generate` warmup, the VLM chat warmup, and the PD disaggregation warmup. The sampler then calls `top_k_top_p_sampling_from_probs`, and the module loads before the server is ready.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable. The change does not touch model code, and the server discards the warmup outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot measured.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🦏\n\n<!-